    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d296">

                <pb facs="0464" n="362" sameAs="frus:frus1908/pg362"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 6878/8–10.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of
                            State to Ambassador Hill.</hi><anchor n="1" xml:id="d296-f1"/></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1908-07-24"><hi rendition="#italic">July 24,
                        1908</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 15.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have to inclose herewith, for the
                    information of the embassy, a copy of a dispatch, dated February 5, 1908, from
                    the consul at Tsingtau, China, wherein he requests instructions in regard to the
                    authority of consular officers to issue certain certificates required by the
                    regulations of the colony at Kiaochow to persons who desire to be married; also
                    a copy of the department’s reply dated July 24, 1908, to which is attached a
                    memorandum prepared by the law officer of the department.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Alvey A. Adee.</hi></signed></closer>







